Those examples for what you'd like to use a 'small wish' don't meet my 
criterions of being 'small'. I support the concept of a 'small wish', but
that means that it should indeed not allow you to wish for powerful stuff.
Also, artifact wishing should be strictly limited. I propose to make three 
levels of wishing:

Level 1 wishes:
non-magic items only (i.e. no wands, amulets, rings, magic potions, magic 
scrolls, magic tools); these would allow you to wish for the following items 
only:
 * arbitrary food, 
 * non-blessed/rustproofed/enchanted/named weapon, 
 * non-blessed/rustproofed/enchanted normal armor (i.e. no dragon scales, no 
     gauntlets of power/dexterity, no boots of whatever, no shield of 
     reflection, no helm of whatever, no cloak of whatever), 
 * gems,
 * gold (up to e.g. 500?),
 * non-blessed scrolls of blank paper and identify (well, don't know, the 
     latter sounds magic too),
 * non-blessed spellbooks of blank paper,
 * uncursed potions of water,
 * non-blessed potions of juice, 
 * non-blessed/rustproofed/enchanted/named tools (i.e. no unicorn horn, no
     horn/drum/bag of whatever, no crystal balls, no magic marker, no magic
     lamp, etc. etc. [you know what I mean])

Level 2 wishes:
work for any item except for named artifacts (weapons & quest items)

Level 3 wishes:
work for anything not already existing (artifacts) or things unwishable in
the current version (loaded wand of wishing, AoY); however, you have only
3 (three) of these in the whole game, non-rechargable by any means; maybe
you even have none or only one before completing the quest.


Level 2&3 wishes would be granted by similar means as they are granted now
(i.e. fountains, djinnies, WoW, thrones, praying, offering). If you decide 
to make a level 3 wish your counter is permanently decreased independently 
of the success of your wish (e.g. because you wish for an artifact already 
in the game); but of course if your counter is already (or, if you need to 
complete the quest: still) at zero, your wish is wasted. Appropriate warning 
may be given via rumors, oracle or messages when wishing.

Level 1 wishes could be granted from e.g.
  * fountains,
  * wands of small wishing,
  * scrolls of wishing,
  * thrones,
  * praying,
  * offering,
  * quest leader upon returning with the quest artifact,
  * some new artifact.

However the chance of getting a small wish should not be much higher than
getting a "big" one.

Just my 2 cents,
